#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:9
msgid "Single Particle Model with Electrolyte (SPMe)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:21
msgid "Model Equations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:32
msgid ""
"The SPMe comprises an equation for the lithium concentration in a "
"representative particle in the negative electrode :math:`c_{\\text{s,n}}`, "
"an equation for the lithium concentration in a representative particle in "
"the positive electrode :math:`c_{\\text{s,p}}`, and an equation which "
"governs the behaviour of the first-order correction to the lithium "
"concentration in the electrolyte :math:`c_{\\text{e,k}}`. Here we use a "
"roman subscript :math:`\\text{k} \\in \\text{n, s, p}` is used to denote the "
"regions negative electrode, separator, and positive electrode, respectively."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:35
msgid ""
"At the centre of each particle the standard no-flux condition is imposed, "
"and the flux on the surface of the particle is simply the current :math:`I` "
"divided by the thickness of the electrode :math:`L_{\\text{k}}`, as in the "
"SPM. Since lithium is transferred between the electrolyte and particles, the "
"flux through the particle surface also enters the electrolyte diffusion "
"equation as a source/sink term. There is no transfer of lithium between the "
"electrolyte and current collectors, which leads to no flux boundary "
"conditions on the lithium concentration in the electrolyte :math:"
"`c_{\\text{e,k}}` at either end of the cell."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:38
msgid ""
"We must also impose initial conditions which correspond to setting an "
"initial concentration in each particle :math:`c_{\\text{s,k}}(t=0) = "
"c_{\\text{s,k,0}}`, and to having no deviation from the initial (uniform) "
"lithium concentration in the electrolyte :math:`c_{\\text{e,k}}(t=0) =  "
"c_{\\text{e,0}}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:40
msgid "The model equations for the SPMe read:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:43
msgid "Particles:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:45
msgid ""
"\\frac{\\partial c_{\\text{s,k}}}{\\partial t} = -\\frac{1}{r_{\\text{k}}^2} "
"\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial r_{\\text{k}}} \\left(r_{\\text{k}}^2 "
"N_{\\text{s,k}}\\right), \\\\\n"
"N_{\\text{s,k}} = -D_{\\text{s,k}}(c_{\\text{s,k}}) \\frac{\\partial "
"c_{\\text{s,k}}}{\\partial r_{\\text{k}}}, \\quad \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, "
"p},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:51
msgid ""
"N_{\\text{s,k}}\\big|_{r_{\\text{k}}=0} = 0, \\quad \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, "
"p}, \\quad \\ \\ N_{\\text{s,k}}\\big|_{r_{\\text{k}}=R_{\\text{k}}} =\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"          \\frac{I}{Fa_{\\text{n}}L_{\\text{n}}}, \\quad &\\text{k}"
"=\\text{n}, \\\\\n"
"          -\\frac{I}{Fa_{\\text{p}}L_{\\text{p}}}, \\quad &\\text{k}"
"=\\text{p},\n"
"\\end{cases} \\\\"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:60
msgid ""
"where :math:`D_{\\text{s,k}}` is the diffusion coefficient in the solid, :"
"math:`N_{\\text{s,k}}` denotes the flux of lithium ions in the solid "
"particle within the region :math:`\\text{k}`, and :math:`r_{\\text{k}} "
"\\in[0,R_{\\text{k}}]` is the radial coordinate of the particle in "
"electrode :math:`\\text{k}`. All other relevant parameters are given in the "
"table at the end of this notebook."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:63
msgid "Electrolyte:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:65
msgid ""
"\\epsilon_{\\text{k}} \\frac{\\partial c_{\\text{e,k}}}{\\partial t} = -"
"\\frac{\\partial N_{\\text{e,k}}}{\\partial x} +\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"    \\frac{I}{FL_{\\text{n}}}, \\quad &\\text{k}=\\text{n}, \\\\\n"
"    0, \\quad \\\\\\text{k}=\\text{s}, \\\\\n"
"    -\\frac{I}{FL_{\\text{p}}}, \\quad &\\text{k}=\\text{p},\n"
"\\end{cases} \\\\\n"
"N_{\\text{e,k}} = -\\epsilon_{\\text{k}}^{\\text{b}} D_{\\text{e}} "
"\\frac{\\partial c_{\\text{e,k}}}{\\partial x} +\n"
"\\begin{cases}\n"
"      \\frac{x t^+IRT}{F L_{\\text{n}}}, \\quad &\\text{k}=\\text{n} \\\\\n"
"     \\frac{t^+IRT}{F}, \\quad &\\text{k}=\\text{s} \\\\\n"
"     \\frac{(1-x)t^+ IRT}{F L_{\\text{p}}}, \\quad &\\text{k}=\\text{p}\n"
"\\end{cases}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:81
msgid ""
"N_{\\text{e,n}}\\big|_{x=0} = 0, \\quad N_{\\text{e,p}}\\big|_{x=L}=0, \\\\\n"
"c_{\\text{e,k}}(x,0) = 0, \\quad \\text{k} \\in \\text{n, s, p},"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:87
msgid ""
"where :math:`D_{\\text{e}}` is the diffusion coefficient in the solid, :math:"
"`N_{\\text{e,k}}` denotes the flux of lithium ions in the electrolyte within "
"the region :math:`\\text{k}`, and :math:`x\\in[0,L]` is the macroscopic "
"through-cell distance. This equation is also solved subject to continuity of "
"concentration and flux at the electrode/separator interfaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:90
msgid "Voltage Expression"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:92
msgid "The voltage is obtained from the expression:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:94
msgid ""
"V = U_{\\text{eq}} + \\eta_r + \\eta_c + \\Delta\\Phi_{\\text{Elec}} + "
"\\Delta\\Phi_{\\text{Solid}}"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:99
#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:112
msgid "where"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:101
msgid ""
"U_{\\text{eq}} = U_{\\text{p}}(c_{\\text{p}})\\big|_{r_{\\text{p}}=1} - "
"U_{\\text{n}}(c_{\\text{n}})\\big|_{r_{\\text{n}}=1}, \\\\\n"
"\\eta_{r} = -2\\sinh^{-1}\\left(\\frac{I}{\\bar{j}_{\\text{0,p}} "
"L_{\\text{p}}}\\right) - 2\\sinh^{-1}\\left(\\frac{I}{\\bar{j}_{\\text{0,n}} "
"L_{\\text{n}}}\\right), \\\\\n"
"\\eta_c = 2 (1-t^+)\\frac{RT}{F}\\left(\\bar{c}_{\\text{e,p}} - \\bar{c}"
"_{\\text{e,n}}\\right), \\\\\n"
"\\bar{j}_{\\text{0,n}} =  \\frac{1}{L_{\\text{n}}}\\int_0^{L_{\\text{n}}} "
"\\frac{\\gamma_{\\text{n}}}{\\mathcal{C}_{\\text{r,n}}} (c_{\\text{n}})^{1/2}"
"(1-c_{\\text{n}})^{1/2} (1+\\mathcal{C}_{\\text{e}} c_{\\text{e,n}})^{1/2} "
"\\, \\text{d}x,\\\\\n"
"\\bar{j}_{\\text{0,p}} =  \\frac{1}{L_{\\text{p}}}\\int_{1-L_{\\text{p}}}^1 "
"\\frac{\\gamma_{\\text{p}}}{\\mathcal{C}_{\\text{r,p}}} (c_{\\text{p}})^{1/2}"
"(1-c_{\\text{p}})^{1/2} (1+\\mathcal{C}_{\\text{e}} c_{\\text{e,p}})^{1/2} "
"\\, \\text{d}x,\\\\\n"
"\\Delta \\Phi_{\\text{Elec}} = -\\frac{\\mathcal{C}_{\\text{e}}I}"
"{\\gamma_{\\text{e}} \\kappa_{\\text{e}}(1)} \\left(\\frac{L_{\\text{n}}}"
"{3\\epsilon_{\\text{n}}^{\\text{b}}} + \\frac{L_{\\text{s}}}"
"{\\epsilon_{\\text{s}}^{\\text{b}}} + \\frac{L_{\\text{p}}}"
"{3\\epsilon_{\\text{p}}^{\\text{b}}} \\right), \\\\\n"
"\\Delta \\Phi_{\\text{Solid}} = -\\frac{I}{3}\\left(\\frac{L_{\\text{p}}}"
"{\\sigma_{\\text{p}}} + \\frac{L_{\\text{n}}}{\\sigma_{\\text{n}}} \\right),"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/examples/notebooks/models/SPMe.ipynb:114
msgid ""
"\\bar{c}_{\\text{e,n}} = \\frac{1}{L_{\\text{n}}}\\int_0^{L_{\\text{n}}} "
"c_{\\text{e,n}} \\, \\text{d}x, \\quad\n"
"\\bar{c}_{\\text{e,p}} = \\frac{1}{L_{\\text{p}}}\\int_{L-L_{\\text{p}}}^{L} "
"c_{\\text{e,p}} \\, \\text{d}x."
msgstr ""

